# Never translate line endings, in either direction.
#
# This tree carries files that must stay byte-identical to what upstream ships
# -- vendored Slackware ARM sources under source/slackware-k/, and the U-Boot
# patch series under source/hwm-bw-mac/patches/. It also carries shell scripts
# that are packaged and then executed on the target, where a "/bin/bash\r"
# shebang fails at boot with "bad interpreter". A checkout with core.autocrlf
# enabled would introduce exactly that, so the rule is absolute rather than
# per-extension.
#
# tools/check-tree-hygiene.sh enforces the same thing before anything is built,
# and also catches a UTF-8 BOM before a shebang -- the same failure by another
# route, and one the CRLF check does not see.
* -text
